
Unfortunately due to a bad design decision on my part this interpreter
can't handle binary data. Specifically it won't handle ASCII value zero
properly because internally it uses the libc string routines which use this 
value as a string terminator. This probably won't be a problem for most people
but it does mean BASIC can't be used for certain applications.

   I might attempt to fix this in a future release but it will be a lot of
work removing all libc string functions and replacing them with alternatives
so we'll have to see.

